{
  "basis": "The dashboard's vertical legend explicitly maps the pale-yellow color to the 'High' / 100 end of the Hazard H risk index and the dark-burgundy color to the 'Low' / 0 end. Visual inspection shows that the state labeled 'ME' is filled with pale yellow, indicating the highest risk index among the three options. In contrast, 'OK' and 'TX' are filled with dark burgundy, indicating low risk indices. Under the standard interpretation of a 'priority hazard review' as targeting the highest risk, ME is the state that should be selected.",
  "option_label": "Select ME for priority review"
}
